# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Prediction-model runtime and regenerable artifacts
#
# Everything below is either written by a running process or reproducible from
# a documented command. Committing these bloats the repo, embeds one machine's
# state, and -- for the audit trails -- publishes live operational data.
#
# The audit JSONL files are the worst case: mqtt_live_ingestor.py appends to them
# continuously, so `git add -A` would sweep megabytes of live prediction history
# into a commit. They were 13 MB and 2.7 MB and still growing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
prediction-model/data/prediction_audit.jsonl
prediction-model/data/observation_audit.jsonl
prediction-model/data/prediction_audit.jsonl.*
prediction-model/data/observation_audit.jsonl.*

# HTTP fetch caches: regenerate with fetch_current_telemetry.py / fetch_nwp_benchmark.py
prediction-model/data/kloudtrack_history_cache/
prediction-model/data/nwp_fetch_cache/
prediction-model/data/gfs_cache/
prediction-model/data/nwp_benchmark_cache.json

# Refetched telemetry: regenerate with
#   python prediction-model/src/fetch_current_telemetry.py \
#     --start 2026-06-20 --end <today>
# The committed corpus (weather_telemetry.csv) is the release input.
prediction-model/data/weather_telemetry_current.csv

# Experiment outputs. Candidate artifacts that are candidates for release live in
# prediction-model/data/candidate_artifacts/ and ARE tracked; these are the
# scratch arms and ablation runs kept for reproducibility of the analysis.
prediction-model/data/candidate_artifacts_windfix/
prediction-model/data/candidate_artifacts_leaky_olddata/
prediction-model/data/seed_sweep/
prediction-model/data/seed_sweep_analysis.json
prediction-model/data/nwp_benchmark_candidate_*.json
prediction-model/data/nwp_bm_ctrl_*.json

# Stray temp artifacts from interrupted jobs. These appear as FILES as well as
# directories, so the pattern must not end in a slash: `tmp*/` only matches
# directories and a 558 KB file named tmpXXXXXXXX slipped through.
prediction-model/data/tmp*

# Live ingestor output. mqtt_live_ingestor.py rewrites this continuously while
# the service runs, so while it was tracked it dirtied the worktree on every
# publish. That made the provenance gate's read-only-worktree assertion fail
# intermittently -- it passed in isolation and failed in suite order, which is
# the worst possible failure mode for a test you are trying to trust.
prediction-model/data/mqtt_live_predictions.json

# analysis scratch
scratch/
